}'", "description": "List symbols near target addresses"}

{"command": "# No DWARF coverage for those addresses (they're in linker-generated thunk sections)
# These are Cortex-A53 erratum 843419 thunks - they're short branches back to the real function
# The llvm-addr2line already gave us the best answer: mono_interp_exec_method.in_labels
# But since thread is "SGen worker", let's look at what functions are actually near those in the .text

# Let's check the actual .text symbols more carefully
aarch64-linux-gnu-readelf -s /tmp/symbols/libmonosgen-2.0.so.dbg 2>/dev/null | awk '
{
  if ($4 == "FUNC" && $7 != "UND") {
    addr = strtonum("0x"$2)
    size = strtonum($3)
    if (addr <= 0x2f4b20 && addr + size > 0x2f4b20) print "0x2f4b20 in: " $8 " [0x"$2" size "$3"]"
    if (addr <= 0x2f4c84 && addr + size > 0x2f4c84) print "0x2f4c84 in: " $8 " [0x"$2" size "$3"]"
  }
}' | head -10", "description": "Find containing functions via ELF symbol table"}
